The PPA source workflow vendors locked dependencies and pushes generated
source directly to build/ppa in Launchpad's dillo-ppa repository. The
branch exists only on Launchpad. No compilation or GPG signing happens in CI.

Configure https://code.launchpad.net/~nmccallum/+recipe/dillo with:

    # git-build-recipe format 0.4 deb-version {debversion}+{time}
    lp:~nmccallum/pichi-vm/+git/dillo-ppa build/ppa

Select Ubuntu Noble (24.04) and any newer supported releases, disable daily
builds, and target ppa:nmccallum/pichi with amd64 and arm64 enabled.
The workflow requests builds after each main push. Publication is asynchronous.

The repository Actions secret LAUNCHPAD_AUTHORIZATION contains the pichi-vm
OAuth Authorization header, as in Corium. CI obtains a short-lived repository
Git token from Launchpad; no GPG key or separate Git credential is needed.

Build the prepared source offline with dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc.
Noble uses its versioned cargo-1.91 and rustc-1.91 packages; newer Ubuntu can
use its default compiler. Only the host executable is built; VM tests need
separate guest artifacts. The package build checks the executable's --help.
